# Deploy Commands

## TWO ENVIRONMENTS — DEFAULT TO TEST

There are **two installs** of the app on `sg-s2`. **Always deploy to TEST first.** Only deploy to PRODUCTION when the user explicitly says "pull to main site", "deploy to prod", "push live", or similar. Never deploy to production proactively.

| Env | Path | Domain | Branch | Deploy when |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **TEST** *(default)* | `/home/bakeandgrill/test.bakeandgrill.mv` | `test.bakeandgrill.mv` | `main` | Every "pull?" by default |
| **PRODUCTION** *(live site)* | `/home/bakeandgrill/public_html` | `bakeandgrill.mv` (main domain) | `main` | Only when user explicitly asks for production / live / main-site |

If the user just says "pull?" with no environment qualifier → **TEST only**. Confirm before touching production.

## TEST auto-deploy

Preferred path: once-minute cron (`scripts/self-update-test.sh`) pulls `main` after CI is green. Install once:

```bash
cd /home/bakeandgrill/test.bakeandgrill.mv && git pull origin main && bash scripts/install-self-update-cron-test.sh
```

Details: `docs/TEST_AUTO_DEPLOY.md`. Production is never auto-deployed.

## TEST deploy (manual)

**Full deploy** (new migrations or PHP deps):
```bash
cd /home/bakeandgrill/test.bakeandgrill.mv && git pull origin main && cd backend && composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader && php artisan migrate --force && php artisan config:cache && php artisan route:cache && php artisan view:clear && php artisan queue:restart
```

**Quick pull** (frontend/small fixes only — no new migrations):
```bash
cd /home/bakeandgrill/test.bakeandgrill.mv && git pull origin main && cd backend && php artisan config:cache && php artisan route:cache && php artisan view:clear && php artisan queue:restart
```

## PRODUCTION deploy (only when user explicitly asks)

Before running, check what's about to ship:
```bash
cd /home/bakeandgrill/public_html && git fetch origin main && git log --oneline HEAD..origin/main
```

**Full deploy** (new migrations or PHP deps):
```bash
cd /home/bakeandgrill/public_html && git pull origin main && cd backend && composer install --no-dev --optimize-autoloader && php artisan migrate --force && php artisan config:cache && php artisan route:cache && php artisan view:clear && php artisan queue:restart
```

**Quick pull** (frontend/small fixes only — no new migrations):
```bash
cd /home/bakeandgrill/public_html && git pull origin main && cd backend && php artisan config:cache && php artisan route:cache && php artisan view:clear && php artisan queue:restart
```

After a prod deploy, always remind the user to smoke-test the live URL (`https://bakeandgrill.mv`) and check the queue worker on prod (it has its OWN worker process, separate from test):
```bash
ps aux | grep "queue:work redis"
```

